WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:07.120
The SCP Foundation handles all kinds of anomalies
and abnormalities, from horrors beyond thought

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.960
to the most simple cryptids.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.720
It goes without saying that ghosts are included
- after all, every culture has stories about

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.120
ghosts, spirits, and hauntings.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.680
But your average poltergeists are nothing
special to the hardened agents and researchers

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:22.960
of the Foundation.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.280
They’ve seen so many that there have been
studies written on their behaviour - what

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.680
could possibly still be scary about them?

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.520
In 1999, the Foundation found out that the
only thing more terrifying than a ghost is

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.040
the absence of one.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.040
But let’s go back in time a little.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:45.040
Way back in 1961, the Foundation were informed
of a little town in the Mississippi backwoods

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.680
called Pollensbee, allegedly a hotspot for
all sorts of anomalies.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:55.360
The town was mostly owned by the Burnley Family
- a long lineage of magicians, occultists,

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:01.040
and alchemists in the Deep South, their power
so notable even the Foundation of yesteryear

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.440
decided they were better left alone.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.760
After conducting some cursory reconnaissance&nbsp;

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.040
on the famous patriarch of&nbsp;
the family, a heresiographer

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.640
named Lyle Alan Burnley, and the ancestral
estate of Elelín, the Foundation decided

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.720
to leave Pollensbee for another day.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.400
That day came in 1978.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.080
Lyle Alan Burnley died, and the estate passed
into the hands of the municipal government.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.560
That’s where the Foundation stepped in - they
had heard lots of stories from frightened

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.720
tourists of Elelín being haunted, of the
land being cursed.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.680
They took ownership and, to their shock, found
that these weren’t just the ravings of spooked

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:40.640
travelers.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.840
Elelín really was haunted, but these ghosts
weren’t hateful or malicious.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:50.560
They were barely even significant enough to
be worth containment - so the Foundation decided

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.840
not to waste their resources on containing
an entire estate.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.960
They cut a deal with the surviving Burnleys:
so long as they made sure the “Revenants”

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.280
of Burnley Manor stayed in line, the Foundation
wouldn’t bother them.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.880
This worked great, all the way until the fateful
year of 1999.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.600
None of the Burnleys remained in the dilapidated
mansion anymore, and the Foundation began

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:20.240
receiving reports of a new anomaly - classified
as SCP-6274.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.720
The ghosts of the Burnley Estate were lashing&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.800
out - and then disappearing,&nbsp;
defying the Foundation’s

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.120
understanding of how ghosts work.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.360
An excerpt written by Lyle Alan Burnley regarding
the hauntings says:

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.960
No two hauntings are quite alike, though they
share some common properties.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:44.880
Let us dispel the notion that all are translucent
people wandering around after dark to scare

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.840
children - a Revenant can take any number
of forms, from a phenomenon to a place.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.440
While I cannot speak for all of them, those
that I encountered in my home life at the

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.760
Estate were universally positive, and helpful
to a fault.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.440
The most universal property being that they
do not leave.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.720
The occultists of yore thought that spirits
could be banished or exorcised.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.400
They were incorrect.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.600
In the decades since Society learned of their
existence, methods have been proposed and

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.160
tested to permanently remove them.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.640
All are prohibitively expensive, and none
have ever worked.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:28.320
At best, their actions can be temporarily
dampened - but they will never go away.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.600
A crew from MTF Mu-13 were sent into Elelin
to investigate the situation.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.880
They enter to find the entire sprawling mansion
without power and in disrepair, the paint

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:40.880
peeling and the roofs collapsing.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.200
They advance through the building, putting
down surveillance cameras and microphones,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.520
trying to find the status of the ghosts.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.800
They find a door to the wine cellar that,
against all force, just won’t open.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.520
Behind it: the sounds of breathing.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:00.560
With no choice, they draw a rune on the door
and leave, finding a dining hall filled with

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:01.680
rotten food.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.800
On their way back - the rune has been erased.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.680
They reassure themselves that there is nothing
to be afraid of, and continue into the main

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:10.400
hall.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.320
That’s when it hits them - the ghosts of
Elelín are awake.

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.640
They see horrifying apparitions on their way
through to the other wing of the mansion,

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.680
where many of the doors are barred from the
inside.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:28.240
The one that isn’t contains a fancy covered
bed and dozens of candles covering every surface.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:31.520
Somehow, they don’t realize one of them
has gone missing.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.440
Then something happens - something bad.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:40.960
The entire section of the documentation is
expunged - when it clears up, two agents are

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.280
reporting waking up in the garden, holding
a book and looking at a tree growing around

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.560
a human body.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:52.160
They rush back to the house and into the kitchen,
but the house has changed from the inside.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:56.640
They find the body of the absent agent, and
a single finger coming from the bottom of

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.000
the sealed door.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.720
The documentation expunges itself just as
the surviving agent arms herself.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:08.080
When it ends, all there is left to do is for
the agent’s body to be recovered hours later

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.720
from the porch, along with the book.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:16.320
The sacrifice of the agents lets the Foundation
discover a few things - the dining room, the

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:23.040
bedroom, and the tree are the sites of Elelín’s
last ghosts - the Feast, the Brood, and the

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:23.760
Totem.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.040
The book seems to be a diary written by Mr.
Burnley, recording all the ghosts of the manor

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:32.720
and their history, and dedicated to his four
children.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.800
The Foundation prepares one of their mediums
- they must commune with the ghosts of Elelín.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.000
First comes the Feast;
The Feast is an entity inhabiting the Silverton

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.640
dining room, among the most docile of those
that inhabit our home.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:53.680
As a boy, it was a favorite plaything — as
a young man, an endless source of amazement

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.560
for the ladies of the town when they came
up to the manor — as an older man, a close

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.200
confidante for when one wishes to shut out
the troubles of the world with food and drink

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:04.720
without conversation.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.760
It is an arrangement of&nbsp;
delicacies and perfectly-cooked&nbsp;

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.400
meats with aged wines and all manner of side

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.120
dishes.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:15.040
Roasted hams, seared steaks, cooked goose
and veal.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.000
The exact contents change regularly — I
remember Arthur and I at breakfasts, making

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.040
a game of guessing what would be on the table
by nightfall.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:29.200
He adored the room nearly as much as I. Like
many other Revenants in Elelín, it seeks

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:35.040
only to live in happy coexistence with the
current generation of Burnleys inhabiting

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:35.920
the home.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:40.400
For the Feast, this means providing delicious
food, and the enjoyment that comes from a

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:41.440
full belly.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.480
After much time in the family's archives in
the Library, I've ventured forth a guess that

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:54.240
the Feast was once Abraham Burnley, a noted
gastronome and gourmet, dead in 1845.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:59.920
I have had little luck in communing with him
in the usual method — it seems he is happy

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.920
to limit his interaction with the world to
one's taste buds.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.920
The Feast is a food-based Revenant - despite
Mr. Burnley’s claims, all it produces now

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:15.760
is rotten, maggot-ridden food filled with
razor blades, shrapnel, and bugs.

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:22.080
The Foundation’s medium, known only as Z,
sits down and begins the ritual in the dining

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:22.640
room.

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:29.120
Her cries are met with small shifts - a plate
moving, meat falling apart, a breeze.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:35.040
Suddenly, she announces to her guards that
something is wrong - that there is no ghost.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.280
An impossibly old voice speaks through her
and to her.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:44.640
It tells her: There is no spirit to be found
here.

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.480
Only absences.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.200
Only nothing.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.400
There is nothing to be afraid of in the dark.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:59.200
Then, in a whisper - that the cellar can only
be opened by the masters of the house.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:04.160
Then the ritual breaks, and all parties look
to the table - where there are hundreds of

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.240
glasses of a dark wine.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:10.320
Since then, the Feast hasn’t shown any activity.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:15.760
A misconception — that ghosts, spirits,
revenants, whatever you choose to call them,

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:20.160
are utterly and totally divorced from the
world which we inhabit.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:26.560
That their interaction is limited to that
of a common poltergeist (hah!), throwing vases

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:30.160
and banging together pots and pans like a
choleric child.

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:31.360
Not so.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.960
Revenants are not altogether unlike living
humans.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.800
They feel emotion.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:41.600
They are driven by something, though they
do not know what (one could say this goes

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:43.200
for most all creatures).

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.480
They rage when they are upset — when they
are angry, bitter, frightened of something.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:54.160
A wise man I met in Jordan some years ago
told me that every Revenant is anchored by

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:59.360
something in the living world - be it a person,
an object, a location.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.520
Something that they left behind.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.600
When this anchor is removed…

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.080
the Revenant ceases to exist.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:08.480
What remains is something else.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:13.680
Then comes the Brood;
As a child I was warned against going into

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:15.760
the bedroom in the western wing.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.520
We all knew the one.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:22.960
It was never locked (Burnleys do not believe
in stifling exploration) but I was told quite

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:28.880
sternly by my father that I would be solely
and entirely responsible for what I found

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:29.760
inside.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:34.160
Decades later, I told Matilda the same thing
when she asked what was inside.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:36.720
Naturally, it stopped neither of us.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:41.760
None of the Revenants in Burnley Manor are
dangerous, but a fair few simply wish to be

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:42.880
left alone.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:48.400
The Brood is one of these — I have no idea
how old it is.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.800
I have asked everyone and searched to the
bottom of the archives, but no one seems to

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.400
know where it came from.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.840
Presumably it does not predate the creation
of the western wing itself in 1798, but who

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.120
can say for certain?

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:06.240
The Brood takes the form of a woman in the
throes of childbirth in her bedchambers.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:10.800
She screams, cries, and generally spurns visitors
(reasonably enough).

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.840
The curtains open for only a few seconds,
but in those seconds any questions you ask

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:19.600
the poor thing are answered with all the truth
of the universe.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:23.920
My father was right — knowledge is not a
burden a child should bear.

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:29.120
Not a day goes by where I do not remember
Matilda weeping as she hugged me.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:32.640
All the Brood does now is&nbsp;
sit inside the impenetrable&nbsp;

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:36.080
bed, constantly softly weeping and occasionally

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:41.280
throwing an object from inside the curtains
- though never daring to open them.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:46.640
Z navigates through the candles and kneels
by the foot of the bed, requesting an audience,

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:52.160
only to be met with a flung baby rattle and
a woman’s soft voice asking who’s there,

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:58.960
demanding where her family has gone, and begging
for help - because nothing’s coming out.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:04.800
Before Z can even respond, the woman inside
the bed screams for her to get the gun - then

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:07.360
the room goes completely dark.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:12.800
The same ancient voice speaks from behind
the curtains: it informs her that she wastes

00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:18.480
her time with ghosts of ghosts while Burnley
Manor is eaten around her - what has killed

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.320
the ghosts of Elelin, impossible as it may
be?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.600
And what does a ghost leave behind when killed?

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:31.760
Once again, just as Z gets her wits, the spell
is broken and the curtains of the bed open,

00:11:31.760 --> 00:11:35.040
revealing a burned corpse huddled under the
sheets.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:38.240
The Brood, too, has fallen silent.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.640
The Burnley ghosts are like no other.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.960
'Haunted manors' are a dime a dozen.

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:48.320
Revenants angry they have been forgotten by
the world, acting out and crowd of unknowing

00:11:48.320 --> 00:11:50.400
fools furthering their suffering.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.400
A tragic story, by any angle.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:57.280
But here — our ghosts are not unknowns,
forgotten by the world.

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:02.960
They are remembered — Burnleys do not shy
away from our ghosts, we approach them with

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.080
open arms.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:10.960
They may be not of this mortal coil, but they
are still family, and family is the most important

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:11.680
thing.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:14.640
Family is what we leave behind in this world.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.960
Our legacy and our mark.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.960
We also leave behind our spirits - our Revenants.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:25.760
This book is a collection of the ghosts of
Burnley Manor and the place they hold in our

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:26.480
family.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.880
The family is the anchor for all of them.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:35.600
I do not like to imagine a world in which
that anchor no longer exists, and so I shall

00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:36.240
not.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:42.240
But when I walk the grounds at night — my
children have all but gone — I realize I

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:44.960
may very well be the last Burnley.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.920
Without me, what will happen to this place?

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:54.480
The memories I have forged here with my children
— my place is to remember what my ancestors

00:12:54.480 --> 00:12:55.920
have left behind.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:58.400
What will I leave behind?

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:03.520
And the Totem;
The Totem is a strange thing.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:08.160
I remember long afternoons spent running through
the gardens with my brothers and sisters.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.400
The groundskeeper hated us, how we would ruin
his perfectly tended shrubs.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:16.800
Then we'd be called in for dinner by the maid,
and wolf down the Feast — before spending

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.880
the evening lounging beneath the Totem.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:22.800
My grandfather sat me on his lap and told
me its story one day.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.520
His own grand-uncle had done a service for
the Indians that still dominated our land

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:28.320
back then.

00:13:28.320 --> 00:13:33.200
The specifics of the service are unclear to
me - but it was great enough that when he

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:38.720
died, they paid their debt, and he came back,
as a sapling in the grounds of the garden

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:40.400
that he loved so much.

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:45.600
The fruit he produced were one-of-a-kind - a
large, round thing the size of your fist with

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:49.120
a thick purple skin and a juicy red inside.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:55.200
He was our oldest family member - we adored
his stories, regaling us with cowboy tales,

00:13:55.200 --> 00:14:00.320
and he was a tree in spirit - happy to watch
the world grow around him.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:05.280
The third ghost of Elelin sits on the far
edge of the gardens, closed off in its own

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:11.120
little pen - the trunk of the tree intertwined
with that of a man, his arm reaching out like

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.440
a branch before being swallowed up by the
wood growing around him again.

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:21.440
The roots and vines have been seen strangling
and choking unwary animals and personnel,

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:25.040
dragging them into the corrosive soil for
digestion.

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:29.120
As such, Z’s communications were performed
from a small drone.

00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:35.200
To everyone’s surprise, the Totem speaks
-- affirming he was once a Burnley, but is

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:39.440
now only a hole, a gap in the shape of a Burnley.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:44.320
Not unlike the rest of the house - once it
was filled with the ghosts and Revenants of

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:48.000
old members of the Burnley clan, but something
happened.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:54.640
The Totem speaks, but its voice ages into
oblivion: Something cosmic turned its eyes

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.560
on a family in Mississippi.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:59.520
Leaving behind nothingness in its wake.

00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:03.920
I was looking through my archives just the
other day when I came across an old journal

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:07.200
of mine, from an expedition into the Ironeye.

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:12.320
They have a rich and ancient culture, and
as with all cultures the aspect of mysticism

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:14.480
and spirituality was strong.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:19.120
I shared my knowledge of certain histories
and heresies, and was provided with their

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.720
own stories in turn.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.160
One story was of a man whose father had been
killed in battle.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:29.680
He was told by a shaman that his father's
spirit, his Revenant, was watching over him,

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:34.320
and would continue to do so for his son and
his son's son and so on.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.320
He was comforted by this knowledge.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:40.240
Many years later, the man was subject to a
curse from a rival House.

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:43.440
Something to plague misfortunes upon his family.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:49.040
In those weeks, he felt a presence by his
side, one he did not even realize was there,

00:15:49.040 --> 00:15:52.000
change - morph from something to nothing.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:59.280
Like a black hole on his shoulder, constantly
pulling — the unignorable presence of nothingness.

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:05.040
The shaman told him plainly — his father's
spirit was no longer the thing walking by

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:06.000
his side.

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.280
It troubles me.

00:16:07.280 --> 00:16:10.240
I have seen what my forefathers have left
behind.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.440
I leave behind four wonderful children and
two wives.

00:16:13.440 --> 00:16:17.760
I leave behind a body of work as impressive
as any scholar of the paranormal.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:21.440
But my children have no interest in the occult.

00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:24.080
The family's secrets will die with me.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:28.000
Whatever I leave behind will be a harbinger
of things to come.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:32.720
Just as the Foundation prepared to give up
the investigation, with all three Revenants

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:37.360
lying indefinitely dormant, a stroke of luck
changed everything.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:43.520
The Foundation was approached by a civilian
- Laura Norman, once known as Laura Burnley,

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:48.240
disowned by her father in the very same will
that left the house to the city.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:52.720
Agreeing to speak with a researcher, she affirmed
that she had tried to avoid her family’s

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.840
legacy and had not seen the house in years.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:17:00.320
The house being haunted was just a simple
fact of life - not something for the Burnley

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:04.880
kids to worry about, but instead housemates
and childhood confidants.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:10.000
Then, she is told that against all logic,
the ghosts of Burnley Manor have been corrupted

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:10.960
and killed.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:16.080
And that everything her father had written
- and disowned her to free her from - points

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:20.320
to whatever killed them being in the wine
cellar underneath the house.

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:25.200
Laura is in disbelief - not least because
the house does not have a wine cellar.

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:30.240
She agrees to open the door that doesn’t
exist - but before she does, the Foundation

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:36.160
discovers three corpses buried in the grounds
away from the house: those of Henry, Arthur,

00:17:36.160 --> 00:17:41.520
and Matilda Burnley, Laura’s sibling, dead
for only a few months.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:46.640
As Laura prepares to descend, the finger beneath
the door pulls itself back in.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:51.840
Laura steps into the dark stairwell, searching
pointlessly for a light against the wall.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:56.960
As she goes down the stairs, descending into
the inky blackness, Laura tells the handler

00:17:56.960 --> 00:18:01.360
that there was a cellar under the house once
- as a child, her father took her down into

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:05.760
a cavernous empty space and told her he would
build a wine cellar there one day.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:08.560
Then she arrives at the bottom, discovering…

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.080
nothing.

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.480
Not just an empty space.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:17.520
But truly, nothing - the cellar is an endless
abyss.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:23.680
As she stares out into the void, the realization
hits her: there is no wine cellar, there are

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:28.640
no ghosts, merely the spaces and outlines
where they should be.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:34.240
Something has consumed the Burnley Manor - and
the last thing the researchers hear before

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:40.480
her microphone cuts out is an ancient voice
behind her, assuring her there is nothing

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:41.840
to be afraid of.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:44.080
And her response: “Dad?”

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:51.200
Now go check out “SCP-2698 Haunted Victorian
Mansion” and “SCP-4153 - Haunted House

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:56.880
Horror - It Came from Site-9!” for more
anomalously chilling haunted house locations!

